 "problems": [
  "Direct HTTP access to senate.gov was blocked by this environment's egress proxy; all pages were read through the web-fetch tool, which summarizes page text with a model. Each member list was checked against the page's official Yea/Nay/Not Voting totals, and all matched. For roughly half the 119th-Congress votes the page was queried for the exceptions to party-line voting (plus not-voting senators and both Alabama senators), and the full roster was rebuilt from those; the rebuilt totals matched the official totals in every case.",
  "The vote_menu_118_1.htm page was truncated in the fetch tool, so May 2023 votes were located by search and confirmed on their individual vote pages (roll 109, 135).",
  "Katie Britt was not in the Senate until Jan. 3, 2023, so she has no recorded votes on the Jan. 6–7, 2021 certification objections.",
  "Tuberville did not vote (recorded 'Not Voting') on roll 118-2-154 (Apr. 23, 2024, Israel/Ukraine/Indo-Pacific/TikTok supplemental).",
  "Several key votes were not simple passage votes: 118-2-39, 118-2-230, 119-1-22, 119-1-644, 119-2-231 and 119-2-253 were cloture on the motion to proceed; 118-2-114 and 118-2-154 were motions to concur; 118-2-292, 119-1-328, 119-1-454 and 119-2-252 were motions to discharge. Titles in keyvotes.json for 118-2-39, 118-2-114 and 118-2-154 describe the question imprecisely (see verify_notes there).",
  "Tie on 119-1-372 (H.R. 1): the vote was 50–50 among senators, and the Vice President's tie-breaking Yea gives the official 51–50. Party totals here count senators only."
 ],
